\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Narrative character-length distribution across three balanced $N{=}1{,}000$ subsets (seeds 1--3, different colours). The dashed line marks the 250-character evaluation limit; the solid line marks 500 characters. Distributions are consistent across seeds, confirming reproducible sampling. Most narratives fall below 300 characters, justifying 250 as a meaningful short-text evaluation point and 500 as the full-length cutoff.}}{4}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:char_hist}{{2}{4}{Narrative character-length distribution across three balanced $N{=}1{,}000$ subsets (seeds 1--3, different colours). The dashed line marks the 250-character evaluation limit; the solid line marks 500 characters. Distributions are consistent across seeds, confirming reproducible sampling. Most narratives fall below 300 characters, justifying 250 as a meaningful short-text evaluation point and 500 as the full-length cutoff}{figure.2}{}}
